1
00:00:00,310 --> 00:00:02,150
The Eiffel Tower is taller in summer.

2
00:00:02,150 --> 00:00:03,750
Shorter in winter.

3
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:05,350
How is that possible?

4
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:08,250
To understand why, look beyond the landmark

5
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:11,550
to the iron that forms its structure.

6
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:15,300
When iron heats up, it expands a little.

7
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:17,400
In other words, it gets bigger.

8
00:00:17,530 --> 00:00:19,100
In a small piece of iron,

9
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,150
the change is barely visible.

10
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:23,400
But the Eiffel Tower’s structure

11
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,250
responds to that same heat,

12
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:26,900
and becomes slightly taller.

13
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:29,950
When it gets cold, the iron contracts.

14
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,950
The tower becomes slightly shorter again.

15
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,050
But there’s more than an up-and-down change…

16
00:00:35,190 --> 00:00:38,350
The sun doesn’t heat every side equally.

17
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:40,000
The sunlit side gets warmer

18
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,800
and expands more.

19
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:42,900
The result?

20
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:45,950
The tower bends very slightly away from the sun.

21
00:00:46,090 --> 00:00:48,250
As if it’s leaning away from the sunlight.

22
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:51,950
As the sun moves, the direction changes too.

23
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,100
But this movement is so small

24
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:56,850
you won’t notice it standing below the tower.

25
00:00:56,990 --> 00:00:58,600
This is a natural response of the structure.

26
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:01,150
By itself, it isn’t a sign of damage.

27
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:04,000
So the tower that looks perfectly still in photos

28
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,650
is responding throughout the day.

29
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:08,550
Before this video, did you think

30
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:11,622
a metal tower could change size with heat?
